1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:04,464
We've sure grown up a lot since
that summer in the digital world.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:07,957
Tai's in high school,

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,997
my brother Matt's trying
to be a rock star,

4
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,817
Sora's become quite a tennis
player, Izzy's in high school too,

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,597
Mimi and her folks moved to New York,
and Joe's still studying to be a doctor.

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:20,268
But for Kari and I,
it's just the beginning.

7
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:41,817
Oh, yeah, yeah,

8
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,197
yeah, yeah,

9
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:50,280
yeah.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,397
Am I not yet? I did now. I'm in here.

11
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,060
Do it again.

12
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:16,160
And it goes in the inside.

13
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:20,260
And near the target.

14
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:22,018
I can't wait to go.

15
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,253
And I'm standing there.

16
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:29,020
It's now.

17
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:32,717
I've forgotten the tomorrow,

18
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:37,600
I'll go back and go
back to the next battle!

19
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,360
Run for your lives!

20
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,245
It's the evil Digimon Emperor!

21
00:01:59,020 --> 00:01:59,850
Ah-ha!

22
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,880
That was close.

23
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,197
You're going to be late for school, TK.

24
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,897
Hurry up and finish your breakfast.

25
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:44,560
New school, new apartment, but
the same old lumpy oatmeal.

26
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,100
I'm done, Mom.

27
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,110
I'm leaving.

28
00:02:47,193 --> 00:02:49,737
Sorry I can't drive you to
school on your first day.

29
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,397
But I have to write this
article before the deadline.

30
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,077
It's all about the historical
significance of toilet paper.

31
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,900
Hmm, it's okay. I'll walk.

32
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,390
See you later

33
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,502
How's it going?

34
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,042
Fine, thank you

35
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,490
Great,

36
00:03:07,573 --> 00:03:11,317
my name's TK And my mom and I just moved
into this building I'm in 7th grade,

37
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:14,080
Class A Nice to meet you Oh, hi,

38
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,617
my name is Yoli Would you like
to walk to school with us?

39
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:21,077
It takes exactly 12.3 minutes And that's
if there's no wind It'll be fun Oh,

40
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,101
and this is Cody

41
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:24,477
Welcome to the building, TK Come on,

42
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,736
we don't want to be late on
our first day Let's do it.

43
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:33,977
Hey, Yoli, can you come over after
school and fix my computer again?

44
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:36,457
Only if your mom makes
those brownies I love.

45
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:39,737
I'll send an email and ask her if
she'll make a batch right away.

46
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,860
It's a deal. Perfecto. Huh?

47
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,740
Kick it over here.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:46,730
Tai?

49
00:03:46,813 --> 00:03:47,720
I'm seeing things.

50
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,260
Here you go, James.

51
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:55,720
Thanks. Great catch.

52
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,350
Huh?

53
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:00,920
You look familiar.

54
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,536
Must be the goggles.

55
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:03,810
What?

56
00:04:03,893 --> 00:04:05,597
Hey, Davis, you're holding up the game!

57
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,510
Yeah!

58
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:07,490
Huh?

59
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:08,890
Yeah!

60
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,638
What am I thinking?

61
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,000
That can't be Tai.

62
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,877
He's a much better soccer
player than that kid.

63
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,790
Where did you see?

64
00:04:14,873 --> 00:04:15,703
I got it!

65
00:04:15,786 --> 00:04:16,616
I got it! Come on!

66
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:17,790
Pass it!

67
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,598
All right, with luck, you're
in my class again, Kari.

68
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,737
I wouldn't call that luck.

69
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:27,100
Hey, the weirdest thing just happened.

70
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:29,157
This new kid said I
reminded him of someone.

71
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,820
Probably thinks I'm a movie star. Yes.

72
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:35,160
Hi, help! Hi!

73
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:38,610
Huh?

74
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,540
I'm Mr. Hamasaki.

75
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:45,880
I'll be your teacher, and I'd like
you all to welcome a new student.

76
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,030
Whoa!

77
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:48,660
It's nice to meet you.

78
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,840
I'm TK. It's that kid.

79
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:55,160
Please take a seat next to the girl
with the camera around her neck.

80
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,680
Together again.

81
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:59,076
Just like old times.

82
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,737
That kid's trying to
make a move on my girl.

83
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,960
Our teacher looks like Ogre-mon.

84
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,090
Hurry!

85
00:05:09,173 --> 00:05:10,747
Don't let Snimon catch us!

86
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:15,617
This praying mantis Digimon can cut through
anything with his twin-sickles attack!

87
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:16,680
Twin-sickles!

88
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,880
Oh, no! Be-o-mon! Tickle-mon! Ogre-mon!

89
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,660
Tai, you're here!

90
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,020
You've got to digivolve!

91
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,230
Huh?

92
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,597
That's why I need your help, Tai!

93
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,060
I can't digivolve!

94
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,377
Did you forget how?

95
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:40,342
It's just like riding a bicycle,
now start pedaling and digivolve!

96
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:46,300
It's no use, as long as I
have the black digivice.

97
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,360
There's no way they can digivolve.

98
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:55,680
Move your tail!

99
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,397
We're gonna need more help.

100
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,245
I'd better contact the others.

101
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:06,810
Huh?

102
00:06:06,893 --> 00:06:08,237
Come to the digital world right away.

103
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,457
The Digimon need our help.

104
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:11,057
Must be a link to an online game.

105
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,434
Let's see who sent it.

106
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:13,650
Tai Kamiya.

107
00:06:13,733 --> 00:06:16,177
Hey, there's a girl in the seventh
grade with the same last name.

108
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,848
This email's probably hers.

109
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,177
So, TK, how does your mom
like the new apartment?

110
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:21,237
She hasn't seen it yet.

111
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,797
She's been on the computer the whole time.

112
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:23,760
Hey, buddy.

113
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:26,160
His name is not Buddy. It's TK.

114
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:30,740
All right, TJ or JB or whatever
it is, how do you know Kari?

115
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,510
Huh?

116
00:06:32,593 --> 00:06:33,423
How do I know her?

117
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:34,957
Well, I get it.

118
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,275
You're jealous of me.

119
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:38,100
I'm not jealous of anybody.

120
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,470
Hey!

121
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,100
Oh, hi, Yoli.

122
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,560
You're Kari Kamiya, aren't you?

123
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:45,737
Yeah, that's right.

124
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:46,697
Why do you ask?

125
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:48,540
Well, are you related to Tai?

126
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:49,898
He sent this email.

127
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,660
My brother needs us.

128
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:58,437
Hey, Yoli, I'm glad I found you.

129
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,537
I need to use the
computer room right away.

130
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:04,577
You mean the legendary former computer
club president is actually looking for me?

131
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:05,490
I'm honored.

132
00:07:05,573 --> 00:07:06,403
What's up, Izzy?

133
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,268
Tai sent us an urgent email.

134
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:09,770
Yeah, I know.

135
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,040
I got one too.

136
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:17,128
I was just about to send Tai an answer
when the battery ran out of my computer.

137
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:20,277
I knew I should have
recharged it after I played

138
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,537
trigonometry trivia on
the Internet last night.

139
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:25,020
But, boy, talk about fun.

140
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,300
I got him!

141
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:27,960
It's from Izzy.

142
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,240
He's got Kari and TK with him.

143
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,840
Tai, come here, quick!

144
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,177
What's the Digital World?

145
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,617
Is that a new amusement park?

146
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,641
I bet they have some great rides.

147
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,477
I heard about it from Tai once.

148
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:42,817
He said there were a lot of
Digimon there, whatever they are.

149
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:43,780
You know Tai.

150
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:46,200
They play on the same soccer team.

151
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,920
Hey, guys, I've got an idea.

152
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:50,497
Let's all go to the Digital World.

153
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:52,345
Yoli, weren't you coming over?

154
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,757
Remember, you were gonna fix my computer.

155
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,420
Oh, sorry, I forgot.

156
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,830
It does there.

157
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,937
The gate to the digital world's open.

158
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:00,850
Look at that!

159
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:01,763
That's weird.

160
00:08:01,846 --> 00:08:03,377
It's got the Crest of Courage on it.

161
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:04,290
Is it an egg?

162
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:06,775
I never saw an egg with a spike in it.

163
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:09,737
It must have been rough on the
chicken that laid that thing.

164
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,114
Let's have a closer look at this thing.

165
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,940
They look like fireflies.

166
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,693
We're really fast ones.

167
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,500
You did promise. I know.

168
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,777
We're going back to the digital world.

169
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,690
Prodigis!

170
00:08:29,773 --> 00:08:30,603
I'm going with you.

171
00:08:30,686 --> 00:08:31,679
That's impossible.

172
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,777
Not just anybody can go, you know.

173
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,036
You need a digivice.

174
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:36,990
Listen, TC.

175
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,632
If you can go, so can I.

176
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:49,460
What's this?

177
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:50,637
A digivice.

178
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:53,367
It's a different model
than the ones we have.

179
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:59,517
We'd better go now, while the gate
to the digital world is still open.

180
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:02,012
Yeah, but how long will it stay open for?

181
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,150
I don't care.

182
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,917
I'm going to help my brother.

183
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,177
Hey, can I get Donkey
Madness on this thing?

184
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:08,320
It's not a game.

185
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:11,117
If the digital world sends you a Digivice,

186
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:14,097
then there's a reason, and
you should take it serious.

187
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,840
I'm not waiting any longer.

188
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,120
I'm with you.

189
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:28,456
It's your turn, unless you're scared.

190
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,800
Huh? I'm there!

191
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,490
Whoa!

192
00:09:39,573 --> 00:09:40,517
What's going on in here?

193
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:41,430
Nothing.

194
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:43,949
Izzy, what was that light?

195
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,957
The computer must need a new screensaver.

196
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:46,870
There we go!

197
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:56,560
Whoa, my first time being
downloaded. Pretty cool.

198
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,900
So this is the digital world, huh?

199
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:03,909
Whoa, this place comes
with a new wardrobe.

200
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:08,397
Looks like we have some
visitors in my garden.

201
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,833
And they weren't even on the guest list.

202
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,218
It's over this way.

203
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:31,257
This place doesn't seem so scary.

204
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,177
The way Tai put it through
a monster is everywhere.

205
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,090
Huh?

206
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:35,597
Hey, guys, check it out.

207
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:37,209
There's a vending machine.

208
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:38,914
I am a little thirsty.

209
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:52,817
Ha ha very funny huh so
were those things digimon

210
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,337
yep there's tons of other
ones too a lot cuter

211
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:58,697
than those and a lot
scarier ones too do they all

212
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:01,545
come out of vending
machines they're real close

213
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,450
There!

214
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,670
KK!

215
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,630
Patamon!

216
00:11:07,713 --> 00:11:09,320
Boy, am I glad to see you!

217
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:11,580
Hi, guys.

218
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,520
I'm glad you all made it.

219
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:14,870
Tai!

220
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:17,319
I told those guys you'd be alright.

221
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:21,280
Uh, Davis, what are you doing here? Kari!

222
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,540
Your tail ring.

223
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,180
Tell me what happened.

224
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,790
Hornblaster!

225
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:46,120
One day, this bossy human appeared and
began making Digimon into his slaves.

226
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,520
He said, I am the Digimon Emperor.

227
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:51,937
I heard we're all going to have
to punch a time clock, too.

228
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:52,850
Another human?

229
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:55,397
You mean that someone else
comes here besides us?

230
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,480
Well, there goes the neighborhood.

231
00:11:57,780 --> 00:12:02,721
Yeah, and he's got this strange new dark
digivice that makes us unable to digivolve.

232
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,300
So are yours. Huh?

233
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,500
Like this one? That's it!

234
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,337
You work for the Digimon Emperor!

235
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,250
What?

236
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:11,163
I don't work for anybody.

237
00:12:11,246 --> 00:12:12,437
Besides, mine's not dark.

238
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,677
I just got this thing when
it came out of the computer.

239
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:17,617
So that's what came out of
the egg when I picked it up.

240
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,100
Three new digivices.

241
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:21,120
But why did Davis get one?

242
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,237
What's his purpose in the digital world?

243
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:26,920
And more importantly, who
got the other two digivices?

244
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,975
Where did everyone disappear to, Izzy?

245
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,617
I told you already, Yoli.

246
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:32,530
They went home.

247
00:12:32,613 --> 00:12:34,417
I'm not letting you
off the hook that easy.

248
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,237
I know you're hiding
something from me, Izzy.

249
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:39,337
Now, what is the digital world,
and what exactly are Digimon?

250
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:41,497
I don't know what you're talking about.

251
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:43,227
Finn, what do you call this?

252
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:44,895
Where'd you get that?

253
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,813
Cody's got one as well.

254
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,568
No, Yoli's not coming over.

255
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,497
We have to stay after
school for Computer Club.

256
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:54,257
But since you made the brownies, I'll
come home and pick them up first.

257
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:59,164
The dark Digivice is draining our power
and making us all weak as newborn kittens.

258
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,677
That's why you couldn't Digivolve.

259
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,995
Yeah, if I could Digivolve,
he wouldn't stand a chance.

260
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:09,780
The Digimon Emperor uses these powerful
dark rings to control the Digimon.

261
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:10,957
Yeah, that's right.

262
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:14,460
And once the ring captures
you, you're a slave for life.

263
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,637
These collars do everything
but get rid of fleas.

264
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,720
Digimon Emperor, I'm gonna
